.Dd July 5, 2026
.Dt XTC_LAUNCH 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_launch
.Nd run a function on a fiber with a precise one-shot deadline
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc_launch.h
.Ft int
.Fo xtc_launch
.Fa "xtc_loop_t *loop"
.Fa "xtc_launch_fn fn"
.Fa "void *arg"
.Fa "int64_t timeout_ns"
.Fa "const xtc_launch_opts_t *opts"
.Fa "intptr_t *result"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs
.Fa fn Ns Pf ( Fa arg )
on a child fiber with a one-shot
.Fa timeout_ns
deadline, the native libxtc form of libinger's
.Fn launch f timeout .
It blocks (parks) the calling fiber until
.Fa fn
finishes or the deadline fires.
A
.Dv NULL
.Fa loop
means the loop the caller is currently running on, the natural default
for launching from inside a fiber.
.Pp
If
.Fa fn
completes within the deadline,
.Nm
returns
.Dv XTC_OK
and, when
.Fa result
is non-NULL, stores
.Fa fn Ns 's
.Vt intptr_t
return value.
If
.Fa fn
exceeds the deadline it is cancelled at the deadline: its per-fiber
recovery and at-exit cleanup run, so any locks, file descriptors, or
memory contexts it registered are released with no leak, and
.Nm
returns
.Dv XTC_E_AGAIN
(the runtime's timeout / try-again code).
If
.Fa fn
faults and the fault is contained by the per-fiber recovery,
.Nm
returns
.Dv XTC_E_ABORTED .
A negative
.Fa timeout_ns
means no deadline (a plain awaited spawn).
.Pp
.Fa opts ,
if non-NULL, may set the child proc
.Fa name
(for logs),
.Fa mailbox_cap ,
and the
.Fa loop
index when launched on an executor loop.
.Pp
.Nm
is composable: a launched function may itself call
.Nm .
It must be called from a fiber (it parks the caller).
.Sh CANCELLATION AND UNCOOPERATIVE WORK
.Nm
bounds a
.Em cooperating
function precisely: one that yields, receives, sleeps, or does I/O is
cancelled at its next such point, which for a short deadline is at the
deadline within a bounded slop.
This is the statement-timeout / bounded-work primitive.
.Pp
A purely uncooperative function -- a tight CPU loop with no yield point
at all -- is a harder case.
Involuntary preemption
.Pq Xr xtc_preempt 3
time-slices such a loop so its loop-mates make progress, and a
resume-point kill hook honors a pending cancel the instant the fiber is
next scheduled through a yield.
Reliably bounding a runaway to a
.Em specific
deadline additionally requires the launching fiber's deadline timer to
be serviced ahead of the re-scheduled runaway, which the single-loop
scheduler does not currently guarantee under full monopolization.
For unconditionally bounding untrusted pure-CPU work, offload it to an
OS process with
.Xr xtc_osproc 3 ,
which the kernel preempts.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv XTC_OK
on a clean finish;
.Dv XTC_E_AGAIN
on deadline (cancelled);
.Dv XTC_E_ABORTED
on a contained fault;
.Dv XTC_E_INVAL
for bad arguments;
.Dv XTC_E_NOMEM
or a spawn error otherwise.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_preempt 3 ,
.Xr xtc_proc 3 ,
.Xr xtc_osproc 3
